  "problem_statement": "POSIX thread-specific data registered with a non-NULL pthread key destructor is not cleaned up when the owning thread exits. A worker can successfully associate a non-NULL value and terminate, but the registered callback is never invoked. The destructor must run once for this worker's non-NULL value, receiving that same pointer. Preserve existing key allocation, deletion, and thread-specific association behavior.",
